// SGA (Standard Galactic Alphabet) compact SDF font — data-driven version.
// All 26 glyphs (A-Z) encoded as primitive drawing instructions in flat arrays.
// A unified evaluation loop replaces the 26 separate per-glyph functions,
// eliminating instruction explosion at compile time.
//
// Primitive types: 0=segment, 1=quadratic-bezier, 2=point
// Each primitive = 7 floats: [type, p0.x, p0.y, p1.x, p1.y, p2.x, p2.y]
//   - segment: uses p0, p1  (p2 ignored)
//   - bezier:  uses p0, p1, p2
//   - point:   uses p0       (p1, p2 ignored)

